==Battleground==
*1 [[Cyberhorn]] spawns after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Shibalien]]s spawn, delay 13.33~26.67 seconds<sup>400f~800f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Mistress Celeboodle]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 20~23.33 seconds<sup>600f~700f</sup>.
*5 [[Helmut Krabbe]]s spawn after 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>, delay 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>.
*1 [[Gorilliam]] spawns as the boss after 46.67 seconds<sup>1,400f</sup>.
*1 [[Nimoy Bore]] spawns after 73.33 seconds<sup>2,200f</sup>.

==Strategy==
As all enemies in the stage are [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Alien]] enemies, any [[:Category:Anti-Alien Cats|anti-Alien]] cats will make it much easier, such as [[Psychocat (Rare Cat)|Neo Psychocat/Corrupted Psychocat]] and [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Castaway Cat/Seafarer Cat]]. Having [[Anti-unstarred Alien Treasures|anti-unstarred Alien]] [[Treasure]]s will reduce the magnification of the enemies and make your [[:Category:Meatshield-class Cats|meatshields]] last longer.

A large stack of Castaway Cats and meatshields should be able to perma-[[Freeze|freeze]] all of the enemies, especially as the strongest pushers, Cyberhorn, Nimoy Bore, and Gorilliam all have a shorter range. In the case that the continuous freezes miss, a stack of Psychocats should be able to [[Slow|slow]] the enemies long enough to keep most of your units alive and allow the Castaway Cats/Seafarer Cats to freeze once again.

If your levels are high enough (30+ for all, 20s may work if high enough level Treasures), the easiest strategy is to just spam meatshields like [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Wall Cat]] and [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Wall Cat]] along with Castaway Cat and Psychocat whenever possible. [[Mistress Celeboodle]] should provide sufficient money to upgrade wallet and build up a stack of the aforementioned Cats.

